.TH "HTMLTABLEELEMENT.CAPTION" "3JS" "August 19, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLTableElement.caption \- HTMLTableElement: caption property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]caption\f[B]\f[R] property of the
\f[CR]HTMLTableElement\f[R] interface represents the first
\f[CR]<caption>\f[R] element child of the given \f[CR]<table>\f[R], or
\f[CR]null\f[R] if no such element exists.
.SH VALUE
An \f[CR]HTMLTableCaptionElement\f[R] or \f[CR]null\f[R].
.PP
This property can be assigned, which causes the existing first
\f[CR]<caption>\f[R] element child, if any, to be removed, and the given
value, if it is not \f[CR]null\f[R], to be inserted as the first child.
Therefore, setting \f[CR]null\f[R] has the same effect as calling
\f[CR]deleteCaption()\f[R].
If the assigned value is not an \f[CR]HTMLTableCaptionElement\f[R] or
\f[CR]null\f[R], a \f[CR]TypeError\f[R] is thrown.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[B]if\f[R] (table.caption) {
  \f[I]// Do something with the caption\f[R]
}
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
